      "writtenOn": "2026-08-06T20:33:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is just a coincidence that this works, and it would be better to not depend on it.  Rather, a chassis specifier should go into a JSON file.  I was thinking number, but maybe name would be OK.  (the zones currently being named after a chassis would only work with 1 zone per chassis so can\u0027t use zone name).\n\nThe zones will definitely have to know chassis status to start and stop events based on chassis presence/availability.\n\nI wonder if it would be the best to have a new singleton to track the chassis properties that different classes could then access, as it\u0027s a little strange for a Fan to have access to say the Manager or parent zone class.\n\nAlso, if 1 place has the current status, then nobody needs to do a GetProperty call themselves and can just get the cached values.\n\nIt could check Present by default, and then also Available if that is enabled.",
      "revId": "42a9b16caee2b9725eb4407377be5a088d87f11c",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
